<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">18 December in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 18 December, from 1777 to 1958.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/united-states" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/united-states.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1777 <span class="tih-ago">249 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Americans observe the first national day of thanksgiving</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Continental Congress set aside 18 December as a day of thanksgiving for the victory at Saratoga. It was the first such national observance by the new United States.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/united-states" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/united-states.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1865 <span class="tih-ago">161 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The 13th Amendment abolishing slavery is proclaimed</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Secretary of State William Seward certified that the 13th Amendment had been ratified by the required number of states. It abolished slavery throughout the United States, freeing about four million people.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1912 <span class="tih-ago">114 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">'Piltdown Man' is presented to the Geological Society</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Charles Dawson and Arthur Smith Woodward announced fossils from Piltdown in Sussex as an early human ancestor. In 1953 they were exposed as a forgery combining a human skull and an orang-utan jaw.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-verdun" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-verdun.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1916 <span class="tih-ago">110 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Battle of Verdun ends</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After ten months of fighting, French counter-attacks closed the Battle of Verdun. About 700,000 French and German soldiers were killed, wounded or missing, and the front was almost back where it began.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/german-empire">German Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-verdun">Battle of Verdun</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1958 <span class="tih-ago">68 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The US launches SCORE, the first communications satellite</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An Atlas rocket placed Project SCORE in orbit. The next day it broadcast a recorded Christmas message from President Eisenhower, the first voice transmitted from space.</p></div></li></ol>
